            and Maggie and Jones are tested for both. Each is recessive, so a puppy is affected
            only when it takes the gene from both parents.
            <a href="https://www.royalkennelclub.com/health-and-dog-care/health-dog-care/health/getting-started-with-health-testing-and-screening/understanding-canine-genetics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The registry on what a DNA test actually tells you</a> is
            worth five minutes before you take anybody's word for it, ours included.
            Write to us and the certificates for Maggie and Jones are yours to read. None of that
            paperwork goes online, where a copy could be cloned for another seller's advert.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bl-stub">
          <h3>{T('What A Puppy Has Had Before It Goes')}</h3>
          <p>
            Its first vaccination, its microchip, worming and flea treatment, and a veterinary
            health check. The records travel with the dog on the day.
            <a href="/blue-staffy-health-uk/">The DNA tests, vaccination dates and health records</a> are
            on the health page, with the second vaccination and the booster.
          </p>
        </div>
