          <li><a href={l.href}>{l.anchor}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p>
        Being on the list changes nothing about the price: the delivery figure is worked out
        from the distance, and the first link above is the one to open when your own town is
        not here. Every one of them goes to a page we wrote, not to a directory listing.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('Why We Keep These Pages')}</h3>
      <p>
        Somebody in York asks a different first question from somebody in Inverness, and a
        page written for the drive is more use than a paragraph on this one.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('Eleven Pages, Not Twenty-eight')}</h4>
      <p>
        Our locations file holds twenty-eight rows and eleven of them are indexed. The rest are
        a few words each, and sending you to one would waste your time.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('One of These Is Not a Town')}</h5>
      <p>The last is our breeding dogs' own page, which is why its wording is different.</p>
      <h6>{T('Kennel Note: Distance, not postcode, prices a journey')}</h6>
      <p>Two towns the same drive away cost the same to reach.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 18 guides — standard, picked style S1. A signpost block: no photograph, because the
      pages it points at carry the images. The breed guide is linked from `the-breed` above,
      which rule 15 restored, so this section keeps the blog hub. */}
  <section id="guides" data-section-label="The long reads, if you want the detail" class={box('guides')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('The Long Reads, If You Want The Detail')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Everything this page states in a sentence is set out at length somewhere else on the
        site, by a page that owns the subject.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <h3>{T('Then The Evidence')}</h3>
      <p>
        <a href="/blue-staffy-blog-guides/">Everything else we have written</a> is the hub for
        the care and breed pieces; the health page and the buying guide are linked from the
        two sections above that own them, which is where a reader meets the question each one
        answers rather than a list of titles at the foot of a page.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('We Would Rather You Read Them First')}</h4>
      <p>
        A reader who has been through the buying guide asks us better questions and gets a
        better answer back.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('Nothing Behind a Sign-up')}</h5>
      <p>Every page here is open, and none of it asks for an address to read.</p>
      <h6>{T('Kennel Note: The guides name us as little as possible')}</h6>
      <p>They are about the breed, not about our litter.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 19 our-happy-blue-staffy-owners-speak — reviews, picked style S2 (review grid on a
      band). The H2 is the migrated page's own (rule 15). All three rows of data/reviews.json
      render here, which is every real review the site has — so the count of
      REVIEW_PLACEHOLDER on this page is zero and nothing is invented to fill a slot. */}
  <section id="our-happy-blue-staffy-owners-speak" data-section-label="Our happy blue Staffy owners speak" class={box('our-happy-blue-staffy-owners-speak')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">Every review we hold</p>
      <h2>{T('Our Happy Blue Staffy Owners Speak')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Three families, named, with the town they live in. That is all of them: we have no
        fourth, and we have not written one.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <Testimonial mode="grid" reviews={allReviews} />
      <img
        class="bl-img"
        src={ownerLondon.file}
        alt={ownerLondon.alt}
        width={ownerLondon.w}
        height={ownerLondon.h}
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <p>
        Each was sent to us by the family who wrote it, and each is kept as a row we can show
        you rather than as a picture of somewhere else.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 20 your-questions-about-blue-staffies-answered — faq, picked style S3 (accordion in a
      card with a jump list beside it). Ten rows of data/faq.json: eight answered from the
      migrated page's own copy and two whose answer IS a setting. The two questions the old
      accordion asked twice are merged into the rows carrying the other wording
      (verbatim.changed). The FAQPage node is built from these same ten. */}
  <section id="your-questions-about-blue-staffies-answered" data-section-label="Your questions about blue Staffies" class={box('your-questions-about-blue-staffies-answered')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('Your Questions About Blue Staffies, Answered')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Considering welcoming a blue Staffy puppy into your home, anywhere across the UK? We’ve compiled answers to the most frequently asked questions by our families. Find quick insights and comprehensive Blue Staffy care and breed guides below.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <p>
        Ten questions, in the order people ask them. The two about money give the same deposit
        and delivery figures as the table further up the page.
      </p>
      <Faq items={faqs} />
      <h4>{T('Every Answer Is One This Page Already Makes')}</h4>
      <p>
        Nothing in the accordion is a claim the sections above have not made, and the two money
        answers match the table.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('Ask Us the One That Is Missing')}</h5>
      <p>Ten rows is not the whole of what we can tell you about a dog we raised.</p>
      <h6>{T('Kennel Note: We answer in 24 to 48 business hours')}</h6>
      <p>That is the window our own FAQ row commits us to, and we hold to it.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="bl-aside">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">In this section</p>
      <ul>
        {faqs.map((r) => <li>{r.q}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </section>

  {/* 21 talk-to-us — standard, picked style S1. The close, and a link rather than a form: one
      enquiry form per money page, and the contact page and the listing carry the site's two.
      The heading replaces a reserve-form label that is live on five other pages, and its
      opening paragraph is DROPPED rather than carried — both rows are in `verbatim.changed`
      with their reasons, and `dropped.text` logs the sentence too. Rule 15 carries the old
      wording UNLESS it states a wrong fact, and that opening states two: it tells the reader
      to fill in details below, and there is no form on this page (one enquiry form per money
      page); and it promises 24 hours, where this site commits to 24-48 BUSINESS hours
      (data/faq.json, the sale-reserve row) on every other page that says so. The real window
      is stated below in fresh prose. No countdown and no scarcity. */}
  <section id="talk-to-us" data-section-label="Come and see them before you decide" class={box('talk-to-us')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('Come And See Them Before You Decide')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Come and meet the litter before you decide anything. Write to us first, we arrange a
        time, and you see the puppies with their mother in the room they were born in. Every
        enquiry is answered within 24 to 48 business hours, by me and not by an agency.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <p>
        <a href="/uk-blue-staffy-breeders-contact/">Write to us, and what to put in the message</a> is
        the page with the site's one enquiry form. If you would rather not use a form, our
        email address is {SITE.email} and messages are read every day, {hours}.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('A Visit Is Arranged, Not Dropped In')}</h3>
      <p>
        There is no kennel with opening hours here. It is a family house, so a visit is
        arranged after we have talked, and somebody is in it when you arrive.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('If The Breed Is Still The Question')}</h3>
      <p>
        Then the breed guide is the honest place to start, not this page. A dog that suits the
        household is worth more to us than a deposit that does not.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('There Is No Newsletter to Join')}</h4>
      <p>
        We keep no subscriber list, so nothing here asks for your address in exchange for a
        page. Write to us when you want to know what is coming and we will tell you.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('One Message Is Enough')}</h5>
      <p>Every enquiry is answered, whatever length it arrives at.</p>
      <h6>{T('Kennel Note: There is no telephone number yet')}</h6>
      <p>We have none to publish, so none is printed rather than a wrong one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageShell>
